From: Samsung OpenHarmony port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] init: initialize SAR ramdisk boot image offset

mount_sar_ramdisk reads rd_offset before its first assignment, so the
computed boot-image ramdisk offset has undefined behavior. Begin the
header/kernel aligned-offset calculation with the header size.

This fixes the fallback loader only; normal bootloader-supplied initramfs
boot is unaffected. No hardware boot validation is claimed.

--- a/init/sar_ramdisk/sar_ramdisk.c
+++ b/init/sar_ramdisk/sar_ramdisk.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ __init int mount_sar_ramdisk(char* name) {
 		goto clean_nobuf;
 	}
 
-	rd_offset += sizeof(header);
+	rd_offset = sizeof(header);
 	rd_offset += padding(sizeof(header), header.page_size);
 	rd_offset += header.kernel_size;
 	rd_offset += padding(header.kernel_size, header.page_size);
